Here's a solution that finds the common elements in two arrays without using any extra data structures. The idea is:

- Sort both arrays in place.
- Use two pointers to walk the sorted arrays and emit elements that appear in both.

This uses no extra data structures beyond the input arrays themselves and runs in O(n log n + m log m) time (due to sorting) plus O(n + m) for the merge pass.

